Not expressible in format 1: each catalog entry (CLUSTER/DATA/NONVSAM header line) owns the indented HISTORY/ATTRIBUTES/... lines below it, and those lines carry 1-4 NAME----value pairs each (plus SYSTEM-TIMESTAMP: whose value is on the next line). Done instead: an entries table (type, name), the per-type "entries processed" totals and the suppressed count as kv, the IDC message lines as a table, and every attribute line as a wide row of key1/value1..key4/value4 (+timestamp) with no link to its entry; section titles, the SHROPTNS flag line, page headers and the command echo are skipped.
